# Sync HTTP endpoints across firmware and docs

When adding, removing, or changing the method, path, or parameters of any HTTP route, update all of the following in the same change:

1. **Web UI API page** — [`ui/src/views/ApiReference.tsx`](ui/src/views/ApiReference.tsx): main endpoint table matches all routes; parameter sections for `/anim`, `/settings`, and `/test/servo` list every supported value and range
2. **API reference** — [`docs/api.md`](docs/api.md): full section per endpoint (curl, JSON, params, errors)
3. **Summaries** — if the endpoint list, params, or boot URLs changed, also update [`README.md`](README.md) and [`docs/hardware/testing.md`](docs/hardware/testing.md)
4. **Route table** — add the route to `kRoutes` in [`src/http/routes.cpp`](src/http/routes.cpp) with its access rule. 404 and 405 answers come from that table

Do not duplicate long behavioral docs (animation behavior tables, RGB LED) in the web UI API page — one-line route descriptions only, except the supported-parameter lists for `/anim`, `/settings`, and `/test/servo`.

Parameter values in the web UI API page must match [`docs/api.md`](docs/api.md) exactly.
